# Salon Backend — Always Follow Existing Structure

Whether the user mentions architecture or not, **match this repo’s patterns**. Do not invent a new layout or DI style.

## Architecture

- Modular monolith (single Express app) — **not** microservices
- **MVRSC** per feature: `model` → `validation` → `repository` → `service` → `controller` → `routes` → `docs` → `index`
- **Module-local DI**: `createShared()` in `src/core/shared.js`; wire modules in `src/routes/index.js` via `createXxxModule(shared)`
- Do **not** reintroduce a central `container.js` unless the user explicitly asks

## Folder map

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/core/` | Infra only (config, database, logger, redis, socket, queue, cron, storage, events, swagger, monitoring, health) |
| `src/common/` | Shared app code (base classes, constants/enums, errors, middleware, helpers, utils) |
| `src/modules/<name>/` | Feature modules — keep the same file shape as `user/` |
| `src/app.js` | Express app factory only (no feature wiring) |
| `src/server.js` | Boot, security middleware, graceful shutdown |
| `src/routes/` | Mount modules + health |
| `src/tests/` | unit / integration / repository / service / controller / socket |

## Coding rules

- Class-based layers; extend `BaseRepository` / `BaseService` / `BaseController` / `BaseValidator`
- DB queries only in repositories; business logic only in services; thin controllers
- Enums only in `src/common/constants/enums.js`
- Cross-module: EventBus + public module factories — never import another module’s model/repository internals
- New module: factory in `modules/x/index.js` → mount in `routes/index.js` → docs in `core/swagger/docs.registry.js`
- Prefer ESM (`"type": "module"`), existing packages, and existing response/error patterns (`ApiResponse`, `AppError`)

## When unsure

Read an existing module (`src/modules/user/`) and mirror it. Do not restructure folders casually.
